commit eb85c6c9b70e25595a9b0882177ce60d910285d4
Author: Liz <liz@gewelf.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 22:03:28 2026 -0400

    perf(read): RowIterator value block in an iterator arena

    Task 2.5, re-measured. rowIterator passes an iterator-owned arena to
    readRowsInternal, so a flat row group's value slices come from one block
    (Row.values_borrowed) instead of one allocation and one free per row. The
    arena is reset when the iterator leaves a row group, which the documented
    contract ("valid until next() crosses a row group boundary") already
    covers. readAllRows and the C/WASM paths keep per-row allocation.

    The earlier drop was for a ~10% mixed5 regression. Five paired runs of two
    prebuilt bench binaries (A = without, B = with), read rows/s, median:
      int64_plain     34.6M -> 41.7M
      f64_plain       33.9M -> 40.6M
      int64_nullable  35.0M -> 41.2M
      str_dict        23.9M -> 26.4M
      str_unique      23.0M -> 25.2M
      mixed5           9.9M -> 10.0M  (A 9.45-10.0, B 9.18-10.15: noise)

    New test drives rowIterator across 3 row groups under std.testing.allocator,
    which exercises the rows_arena branch of assembleFlatRows.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M67V55TADV7E3D595XJPWS1A

 zig-parquet/src/core/dynamic_reader.zig  | 11 +++++++++--
 zig-parquet/src/tests/roundtrip_test.zig | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
commit bde64eb5a50382f70b0908ac144781e7dc5f34f7
Author: Liz <liz@gewelf.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 21:38:44 2026 -0400

    fix(read): projection-aware flat assembly

    readRowsInternal decided between flat and nested assembly by looking at
    every top-level column, so projecting only primitive columns out of a
    schema that also has a nested column went through nested assembly (keeping
    levels and cloning every cell). planFlatLeaves now considers only the
    requested columns and maps each to its leaf index (TopColInfo.leaf_start),
    and assembleFlatRows indexes column_values by that leaf index. This makes
    the old `num_leaf_columns == num_top` guard unnecessary; a leaf missing
    from the row group falls back to nested assembly as before.

    The schema walk (buildTopInfos) and flat column decode (readFlatColumns)
    are split out so the streaming iterator can reuse them.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M67SQWMGSTE28KEEREMFQ8Z1
